    "status": "draft",
    "summary": "Repairs F-028: the WAL writer could not tell a dropped entry sender from the marker that ends a healthy stream, so a truncated append was acknowledged and notified as a success. The writer now names the truncation on both channels and ends, and every adapter call path that panicked or waited on a terminal writer returns a named storage error instead. Amends 001 and 008 and carries their acceptance.\n",
